# Obsidian per-machine UI state (churns constantly — do not sync)
# The rest of .obsidian/ is meant to be TRACKED: plugins + their settings then clone to
# every new machine, so machine #2 installs nothing by hand (D15).
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.obsidian/cache
# graph.json mixes settled config (filter, colorGroups) with per-session UI state
# (`scale` = zoom, `close` = panel open) that every machine rewrites. Ship a
# graph.json.example seed instead and copy it into place per machine. See D15.
.obsidian/graph.json
.trash/

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Secrets — never commit
.env
*.env
.env.*
secrets/
*.key
*.pem

# Private subtree — LOCAL ONLY, never pushed to GitHub
Private/*
!Private/README.md

# Large media — uncomment if you offload binaries to R2/LFS instead of committing
# attachments/**/*.mp4
# attachments/**/*.mov
# attachments/**/*.zip

# Accidental empty canvases created from the Canvas ribbon
Untitled*.canvas

# AIOS per-machine config + scripts (machine-specific; no secrets — keep the .example, ignore the real one)
# config.json holds an ABSOLUTE vault path, which differs per machine (usernames differ) —
# committing it makes every other machine resolve a path that does not exist, silently.
.aios/attachments.json
.aios/config.json
.aios/*.sh
